<span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Forward transition rate, i.e., Eq. (</span><a href="#S3.E7" title="In Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">), from state </span><math id="A1.T2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> to </span><math id="A1.T2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">. This follows the ordering of the conditional distribution </span><math id="A1.T2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, which is the </span><span id="A1.T2.4.15.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">transpose</span><sp