<span id="A1.T2.4.18.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.4.18.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Truncated version of </span><math id="A1.T2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.18.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with threshold </span><math id="A1.T2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.18.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, Eq. (</span><a href="#S5.E18" title="In Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a><span id="A1.T2.4.18.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">)</span></span>
