<td id="A1.T2.4.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.4.20.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:258.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.4.20.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.4.20.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Upper bound on </span><math id="A1.T2.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.20.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="A1.T2.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}})\cdot K/(T-t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}})\cdot K/(T-t)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.4.20.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, Eq. (</span><a href="#S5.E17" title="In Lemma 5.1 (Bound of the outgoing rate). ‣ The comparison of computational complexity and outgoing rate. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity