<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>The Formulations of the Forward Process</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Semigroup Formulation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In general, the time-homogeneous CTMC
can be described by a Markov semigroup <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})=\mathbb{E}\left[f({\mathbf{y}}_{t})|{\mathbf{y}}_{0}={\bm{y}}\right]=\left&lt;f,q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})=\mathbb{E}\left[f({\mathbf{y}}_{t})|{\mathbf{y}}_{0}={\bm{y}}\right]=\left&lt;f,q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon{\mathcal{Y}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon{\mathcal{Y}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Due to the definition, the infinitesimal operator <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> of the time homogeneous <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[f]({\bm{y}})=\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]-f}{t}\right]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;f,\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\Big|_{t=0}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}\coloneqq\left&lt;f,R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[f]({\bm{y}})=\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]-f}{t}\right]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;f,\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\Big|_{t=0}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}\coloneqq\left&lt;f,R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\coloneqq\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\Big|_{t=0}=\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\coloneqq\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\Big|_{t=0}=\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">According to the time-homogeneous property, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})+o(\Delta t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})+o(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, the transition rate function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 0\ \text{when}\ {\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}\quad\text{and}\quad R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>when</mtext><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mtext>and</mtext><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 0\ \text{when}\ {\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}\quad\text{and}\quad R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">due to the definition Eq. (<a href="#A2.E23" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).
Under this setting, we can provide the dynamic of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t|0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t|0}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})={\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}\left[{\mathcal{L}}f\right]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}f,q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[f]({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})={\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}\left[{\mathcal{L}}f\right]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}f,q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[f]({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left[\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}f(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\right]=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left[f(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left[\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}f(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\right]=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left[f(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality follows from the semigroup property.
Combined with the fact</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;f,\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}{\mathcal{Q}}^{\to}_{t}[f]({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;f,\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">derived from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E21" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>),
we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|0}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t|0}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">According to the time-homogeneous property, the above equation can be easily extended to</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|s}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t|s}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{t|s}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t|s}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Combining with Bayes’ Theorem, the transition of the marginal distribution is</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}q^{\to}_{t}}{\mathrm{d}t}({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R({\bm{y}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}q^{\to}_{t}}{\mathrm{d}t}({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R({\bm{y}},\cdot),q^{\to}_{t}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Matrix Formulation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose the support set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be written as <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}=\{{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2},\ldots,{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}=\{{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2},\ldots,{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may consider the marginal distribution <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a vector, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}=\left[q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{1}),q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{2}),\ldots,q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}=\left[q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{1}),q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{2}),\ldots,q_{t}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">conditional transition probability function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a matrix, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\left[\begin{matrix}q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots\\
q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\left[\begin{matrix}q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{1}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{2}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots\\
q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|}|{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> can also be presented as</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\left[\begin{matrix}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots\\
R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\left[\begin{matrix}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots&amp;\ldots\\
R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{1})&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{2})&amp;\ldots&amp;R^{\to}({\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|},{\bm{y}}_{|{\mathcal{Y}}|})\\
\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Under this condition, Eq. (<a href="#A2.E26" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) can be written as</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}/\mathrm{d}t={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}/\mathrm{d}t={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">matching the usual presentation shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen and Ying [2024]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. [2024]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>The Proof of Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">The proof of Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>, the marginal, joint, and conditional distribution w.r.t. <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}^{\leftarrow}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are denoted as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t},\quad({\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t},{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t^{\prime}})\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t,t^{\prime}},\quad\text{and}\quad q^{\leftarrow}_{t^{\prime}|t}=q_{t^{\prime},t}/q_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t},\quad({\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t},{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t^{\prime}})\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t,t^{\prime}},\quad\text{and}\quad q^{\leftarrow}_{t^{\prime}|t}=q_{t^{\prime},t}/q_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">which have <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\leftarrow}_{t}=q^{\to}_{T-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\leftarrow}_{t}=q^{\to}_{T-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we start to check the dynamic of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-1\cdot\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-t|T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-1\cdot\partial_{T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-1\cdot\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-t|T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-1\cdot\partial_{T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\underbrace{\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}}_{\text{Term 1}}-\underbrace{\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}_{\text{Term 2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 1</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 2</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\underbrace{\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}}_{\text{Term 1}}-\underbrace{\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}_{\text{Term 2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">For <span id="A2.SS2.p1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Term 1</span> of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="In The proof of Lemma . ‣ B.2 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>Term 1</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t|T-s}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t|T-s}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equation follows from the Kolmogorov backward theorem (Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma E.3 (Kolmogorov backward theorem, adapted from Theorem 5.11 in [ ] ). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E22" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\cdot)]({\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\left&lt;q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\cdot),R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\cdot)]({\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\left&lt;q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|\cdot),R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">For Term 2 of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="In The proof of Lemma . ‣ B.2 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>Term 2</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}})}\cdot\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equation follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E26" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and the last equation follows from the fact</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})-\delta_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t}\right]\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})-\delta_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t}\right]\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t^{\prime}|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})-\delta_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t^{\prime}-(T-t)}\right]\cdot\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{t^{\prime}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t|t^{\prime}}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{t^{\prime}-(T-t)}\right]=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{t^{\prime}|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\tilde{{\bm{y}}})-\delta_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{t^{\prime}-(T-t)}\right]\cdot\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{q^{\to}_{t^{\prime}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{t^{\prime}\rightarrow T-t}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t|t^{\prime}}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}{t^{\prime}-(T-t)}\right]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">Under this condition, by setting</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\coloneqq R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\coloneqq R(\tilde{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">then Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="In The proof of Lemma . ‣ B.2 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) can be summarized as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\cdot),q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\cdot),q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}(\cdot|{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=\sum_{\tilde{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},\tilde{{\bm{y}}})\cdot q_{t|s}^{\leftarrow}(\tilde{{\bm{y}}}|{\bm{y}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with Bayes’ Theorem, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}{\mathrm{d}t}({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},\cdot),q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}{\mathrm{d}t}({\bm{y}})=\left&lt;R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},\cdot),q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, Eq. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) establishes.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, since the RHS of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Besides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}\left[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}\left[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\left[\partial_{t}(q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}}))\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}+q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\left[\partial_{t}(q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}}))\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}+q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{\partial_{t}q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{s\rightarrow t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{s\rightarrow t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}(q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}}))\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}(q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}}))\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-s}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">The last equation follows from the Kolmogorov backward theorem, i.e., Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma E.3 (Kolmogorov backward theorem, adapted from Theorem 5.11 in [ ] ). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E22" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>)</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\cdot)]({\bm{y}})=-\left&lt;q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\cdot),R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{T-t}q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=-{\mathcal{L}}^{\to}[q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\cdot)]({\bm{y}})=-\left&lt;q^{\to}_{T-s|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|\cdot),R^{\to}(\cdot,{\bm{y}})\right&gt;_{{\mathcal{Y}}}=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with Eq. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=\lim_{s\rightarrow t}\partial_{t}q^{\leftarrow}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}})}{q^{\to}_{T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">when <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Besides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\frac{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex34Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t+\Delta t|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{\Delta t}\right]\cdot\frac{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t+\Delta t|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t+\Delta t|T-t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{\Delta t}\right]\cdot\frac{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{q_{T-t}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\frac{q^{\to}_{T-t+\Delta t|T-t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-\delta_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}({\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\right]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">which means</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}-\left[\frac{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{\Delta t}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}-\left[\frac{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not={\bm{y}}^{\prime}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{\Delta t}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E32" title="In The proof of Lemma . ‣ B.2 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>).
Hence, Eq. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) establishes, and the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>The Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1 (Exponentially decreasing KL divergence between 𝑞^→_𝑡 and 𝑞̃_𝑡). ‣ Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The close solution of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E28" title="In Matrix Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}=\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}={\bm{I}}+t{\bm{R}}^{\to}+\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{2}}{2}+\ldots." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}=\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}={\bm{I}}+t{\bm{R}}^{\to}+\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{2}}{2}+\ldots.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can easily verify that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex37X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}}{\mathrm{d}t}=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to}){\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}\right]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\right]{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}}{\mathrm{d}t}=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to}){\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}\right]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\right]{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">With the following equation,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\right]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}}{i!}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\frac{t^{i-1}}{(i-1)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{j}}{j!}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\right]=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\left[\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}}{i!}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\frac{t^{i-1}}{(i-1)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to})^{i}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\frac{(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})^{j}}{j!}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}}{\mathrm{d}t}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}}{\mathrm{d}t}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the transition rate matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> shown as Eq. (<a href="#A2.E27" title="In Matrix Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) satisfies Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). It can be decomposed as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\cdots\,}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\cdots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑹</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mi>𝑹</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.114em">⊗</mo><mo rspace="0.225em">⋯</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.114em">⊗</mo><mo rspace="0.225em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\cdots\,}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\cdots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kronecker product, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the identity matrix on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to the calculation of the Kronecker product, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{i})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{i})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under this condition, suppose <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)=\{j_{1},j_{2},\ldots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>DiffIdx</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)=\{j_{1},j_{2},\ldots\}</annotation></semantics></math> without loss of generality, for any <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\not\in\{j_{1},j_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\not\in\{j_{1},j_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{2}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{2}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{2}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{2}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Besides, for <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j_{1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{2}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{2}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j_{1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{2}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{2}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">A similar result will be satisfied for <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=j_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=j_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, it has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>when</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, suppose <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)=j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>DiffIdx</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)=j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\not=j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\not=j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{0})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{0})\cdot\ldots\cdot\underbrace{{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})}_{=0}\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Otherwise, when <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j_{1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j_{1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equation establishes since <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{j}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{j}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\not=j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\not=j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, only when <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{j_{1}}=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{j_{1}}=K</annotation></semantics></math>, we will have <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})=1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j_{1}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j_{1}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> due to the definition Eq. (<a href="#A2.E33" title="In Lemma B.2. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>). That means</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\displaystyle\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\ \text{and}\ {\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}\not=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>when</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>DiffIdx</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\displaystyle\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\ \text{and}\ {\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}\not=K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex47Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\displaystyle\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\ \text{and}\ {\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}=K." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>when</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>DiffIdx</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\displaystyle\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\quad\text{when}\quad\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\ \text{and}\ {\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}=K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, suppose <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{1})\cdot\ldots\cdot{\bm{I}}({\bm{y}}_{d},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{d})={\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}_{j})=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}(1-\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{A}}({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}_{j})=-\sum_{i=1}^{d}(1-\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">which implies we have <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=0}^{d-1}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{i=0}^{d-1}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With the decomposition shown in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\ldots\,\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}}}_{d-i\ \text{terms}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\ldots\,\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}}}_{d-i\ \text{terms}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrices <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}={\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}={\bm{R}}_{j}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})=\exp\left(t\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp\left(t{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\right)=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})=\exp\left(t\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp\left(t{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\right)=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, the matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> has the following decomposition, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\ldots\,\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}}}_{d-i\ \text{terms}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">⊗</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}=\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\,\ldots\,\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\text{ terms}}\otimes\,{\bm{A}}\,\otimes\,\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\,\otimes\,{\bm{I}}}_{d-i\ \text{terms}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kronecker product, <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the identity matrix on <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can easily verify that the matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\begin{matrix}-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]=\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&{\bm{0}}\\
-{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]}_{{\bm{U}}}\cdot\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&amp;0\\
{\bm{0}}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]}_{\Lambda}\cdot\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]}_{{\bm{U}}^{-1}}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1}={\bm{U}}^{-1}{\bm{U}}={\bm{I}}_{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>𝑼</mi></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></munder></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑼</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\begin{matrix}-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&amp;{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]=\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&amp;{\bm{0}}\\
-{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]}_{{\bm{U}}}\cdot\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&amp;0\\
{\bm{0}}&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]}_{\Lambda}\cdot\underbrace{\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{I}}_{K-1}&amp;{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{1}}_{1\times(K-1)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]}_{{\bm{U}}^{-1}}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1}={\bm{U}}^{-1}{\bm{U}}={\bm{I}}_{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Under this condition, <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be reformulated as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex55X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes\ldots\otimes({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})}_{i-1\ \text{terms}}\otimes({\bm{U}}\Lambda{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes\ldots({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes\ldots\otimes({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})}_{i-1\ \text{terms}}\otimes({\bm{U}}\Lambda{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})\otimes\ldots({\bm{U}}{\bm{U}}^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left({\bm{U}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{U}}\right)\cdot\left(\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\ \text{terms}}\otimes\Lambda\otimes{\bm{I}}\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right)\cdot\left({\bm{U}}^{-1}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{U}}^{-1}\right)\coloneqq{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑼</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>terms</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left({\bm{U}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{U}}\right)\cdot\left(\underbrace{{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}}_{i-1\ \text{terms}}\otimes\Lambda\otimes{\bm{I}}\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right)\cdot\left({\bm{U}}^{-1}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{U}}^{-1}\right)\coloneqq{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma E.2 (Mixed-product property of Kronecker product). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>.
Under this condition, it has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex56X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\cdot{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\cdot{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}\cdot{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{i}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{U}}^{\otimes d}\cdot\Lambda_{j}\cdot({\bm{U}}^{-1})^{\otimes d}={\bm{R}}^{\to}_{j}\cdot{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the second and forth equations follows from Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma E.2 (Mixed-product property of Kronecker product). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E34" title="In Proof. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the property about the matrix exponential, we start from investigating the case of two commuting matrices, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1}+{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\left({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1}+{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}\right)^{i}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\sum_{j=0}^{i}C_{i}^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1}+{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\left({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1}+{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}\right)^{i}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\sum_{j=0}^{i}C_{i}^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equation establishes since <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are commute.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\sum_{j=0}^{i}C_{i}^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=0}^{i}\frac{1}{i!}\cdot\frac{i!}{j!(i-j)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\sum_{j=0}^{i}C_{i}^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=0}^{i}\frac{1}{i!}\cdot\frac{i!}{j!(i-j)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex58Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=0}^{i}\frac{1}{j!(i-j)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}=\left(\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\frac{({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}}{j!}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2})^{i}}{i!}\right)=\exp({\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to})\cdot\exp({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=0}^{i}\frac{1}{j!(i-j)!}\cdot({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}\cdot({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})^{i-j}=\left(\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\frac{({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{1})^{j}}{j!}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{({\bm{R}}^{\to}_{2})^{i}}{i!}\right)=\exp({\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to})\cdot\exp({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">According to the definition of the matrix exponential, we will have <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})=\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes\exp({\bm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})=\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes\exp({\bm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math> when one of the factors is the identity.
When we multiply all these exponentials, it has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex59X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp({\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to})\cdot\exp({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})=\left[\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right]\cdot\left[{\bm{I}}\otimes\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp({\bm{R}}_{1}^{\to})\cdot\exp({\bm{R}}_{2}^{\to})=\left[\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes{\bm{I}}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right]\cdot\left[{\bm{I}}\otimes\exp({\bm{A}})\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\exp({\bm{A}})\cdot{\bm{I}}\right]\otimes\left[{\bm{I}}\cdot\exp({\bm{A}})\right]\otimes{\bm{I}}\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\exp({\bm{A}})\cdot{\bm{I}}\right]\otimes\left[{\bm{I}}\cdot\exp({\bm{A}})\right]\otimes{\bm{I}}\ldots\otimes{\bm{I}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, following a recursive manner, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(t\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp\left(t{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\right)=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(t\sum_{i=1}^{d}{\bm{R}}^{\to}_{i}\right)=\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp\left(t{\bm{R}}_{i}^{\to}\right)=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">hence the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}-1&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
0&amp;-1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
1&amp;1&amp;\ldots&amp;0\end{matrix}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the matrix exponential <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(t{\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t{\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> becomes</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(t{\bm{A}})=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t{\bm{A}})=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)\coloneqq\exp(t{\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)\coloneqq\exp(t{\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> can be considered as the close solution of the following matrix ODE, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}={\bm{A}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t),\quad\text{where}\quad\bar{{\bm{A}}}(0)={\bm{I}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}={\bm{A}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t),\quad\text{where}\quad\bar{{\bm{A}}}(0)={\bm{I}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">To provide a close form of <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first decompose the matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{B}}&{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{C}}&{\bm{0}}\end{matrix}\right]\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{B}}\coloneqq-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}\in\mathbb{R}^{(K-1)\times(K-1)}\ \text{and}\ {\bm{C}}\coloneqq[1,1,\ldots,1]\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times(K-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑩</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝑪</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}=\left[\begin{matrix}{\bm{B}}&amp;{\bm{0}}\\
{\bm{C}}&amp;{\bm{0}}\end{matrix}\right]\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{B}}\coloneqq-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}\in\mathbb{R}^{(K-1)\times(K-1)}\ \text{and}\ {\bm{C}}\coloneqq[1,1,\ldots,1]\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times(K-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, the ODE. (<a href="#A2.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) can be equivalently think column-by-column, the <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>–th column of <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> solves</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)={\bm{A}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{a}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)={\bm{A}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{a}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">We use the block structure to split <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> into two parts, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)=[\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t),\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}(t)=[\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t),\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{q}}_{1}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{q}}_{1}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{a}}_{K}(t)\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{a}}_{K}(t)\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the last coordinate.
Under this condition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)={\bm{B}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{B}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)={\bm{B}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{B}}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">According to the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{B}}=-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{B}}=-{\bm{I}}_{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)=-\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)\quad\Rightarrow\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)=e^{-t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)=-\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)\quad\Rightarrow\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)=e^{-t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">If we consider the solution of <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, it has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot e^{-t}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot e^{-t}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">For the initial condition, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,\ldots,K-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,\ldots,K-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then it has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=e^{-t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)={\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(t)+{\bm{0}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=e^{-t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(0)+1-e^{-t}=1-e^{-t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(0)+1-e^{-t}=1-e^{-t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">For the initial condition, <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}(0)={\bm{e}}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{C}}\cdot\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{1}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(0)+0=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(t)=\bar{{\bm{a}}}_{K}(0)+0=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(t{\bm{A}})=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t{\bm{A}})=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Forward transition kernel)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the forward CTMC, i.e., <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> with the infinitesimal operator <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\to}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\to}</annotation></semantics></math> given in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). Then, for any two timestamps <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward transition probability satisfies, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E36X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-(t-s)}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-(t-s)}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E36Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-(t-s)})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-(t-s)})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under the matrix presentation, Eq. (<a href="#A2.E25" title="In Semigroup Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) implies the transition matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math> can be considered as the solution of the ODE</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}/\mathrm{d}t={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{s|s}={\bm{I}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}/\mathrm{d}t={\bm{R}}^{\to}\cdot{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}\quad\text{where}\quad{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{s|s}={\bm{I}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\exp\left((t-s){\bm{R}}^{\to}\right)=\exp\left((t-s){\bm{A}}\right)^{\otimes d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\exp\left((t-s){\bm{R}}^{\to}\right)=\exp\left((t-s){\bm{A}}\right)^{\otimes d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-(t-s)}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-(t-s)}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]^{\otimes d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\to}_{t|s}=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-(t-s)}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-(t-s)}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-(t-s)}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]^{\otimes d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">due to the close solution of <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp((t-s){\bm{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp((t-s){\bm{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> shown in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.
Combining this result with the calculation of the Kronecker product Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma E.1 (Basic Kronecker product). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|s}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-(t-s)}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-(t-s)}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex74Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-(t-s)})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\left(1-\delta_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot\delta_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-(t-s)})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">The proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1 (Exponentially decreasing KL divergence between 𝑞^→_𝑡 and 𝑞̃_𝑡). ‣ Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Eq. (<a href="#A2.E28" title="In Matrix Formulation. ‣ B.1 The Formulations of the Forward Process ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), the solution of <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}=\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;e^{-t}&amp;0\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑹</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}=\exp(t{\bm{R}}^{\to})\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}=\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}=\left[\begin{matrix}e^{-t}&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;e^{-t}&amp;0\\
1-e^{-t}&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;\ldots&amp;1-e^{-t}&amp;1\end{matrix}\right]^{\otimes d}\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equation follows from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, the second equation follows from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, and the last equation follows from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.
With the calculation of the Kronecker product Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma E.1 (Basic Kronecker product). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}({\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left[\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}({\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\exp(t{\bm{A}})^{\otimes d}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left[\prod_{i=1}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Under this condition, for any <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote the coordinate set of token <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{i}=K\quad\forall\ i\in{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{i}=K\quad\forall\ i\in{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad{\bm{y}}_{i}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{i}\ \forall\ i\not\in{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad{\bm{y}}_{i}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{i}\ \forall\ i\not\in{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, Eq. (<a href="#A2.E38" title="In The proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) can be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex77X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[\prod_{j\not\in{\mathcal{K}}}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot\prod_{j\not=i}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})(K,{\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[\prod_{j\not\in{\mathcal{K}}}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})\cdot\prod_{j\not=i}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})(K,{\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[\prod_{j=1}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[\prod_{j=1}^{d}\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[e^{-t\cdot|{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})|}\cdot(1-e^{-t})^{|{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}})|}\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}\left[e^{-t\cdot|{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})|}\cdot(1-e^{-t})^{|{\mathcal{K}}({\bm{y}})|}\right]\cdot{\bm{q}}^{\to}_{0}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right))}\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>numK</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>numK</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right))}\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}^{\prime}={\bm{y}}_{{\mathcal{K}}^{c}({\bm{y}})}}{\bm{q}}_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right))),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equation establishes since we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;e^{-t}&amp;&{\bm{y}}_{j}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j}\quad\text{and}\quad{\bm{y}}_{j}\not=K\\
&{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\cdot(1-e^{-t})+(1-{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime}))&amp;&{\bm{y}}_{j}=K\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{aligned}\right.." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t{\bm{A}})({\bm{y}}_{j},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j})=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;e^{-t}&amp;&amp;{\bm{y}}_{j}={\bm{y}}^{\prime}_{j}\quad\text{and}\quad{\bm{y}}_{j}\not=K\\
&amp;{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime})\cdot(1-e^{-t})+(1-{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{j}^{\prime}))&amp;&amp;{\bm{y}}_{j}=K\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{aligned}\right..</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">According to the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can calculate the normalizing constant of <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{Z}_{t}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}}\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))=\sum_{i=0}^{d}\sum_{\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=i}\exp(-t\cdot(d-i))=\sum_{i=1}^{d}C_{d}^{i}\cdot e^{-t\cdot i}=(1+e^{-t})^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></munder><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>numK</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Z}_{t}=\sum_{{\bm{y}}}\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))=\sum_{i=0}^{d}\sum_{\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=i}\exp(-t\cdot(d-i))=\sum_{i=1}^{d}C_{d}^{i}\cdot e^{-t\cdot i}=(1+e^{-t})^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the KL divergence between <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex80X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(q_{t}^{\to}\big\|\tilde{q}_{t}\right)=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{q}_{t}({\bm{y}})}=q_{t}^{\to}([K,\ldots,K])\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}([K,\ldots,K])}{\tilde{q}_{t}([K,\ldots,K])}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{q}_{t}({\bm{y}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ln</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ln</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ln</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(q_{t}^{\to}\big\|\tilde{q}_{t}\right)=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{q}_{t}({\bm{y}})}=q_{t}^{\to}([K,\ldots,K])\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}([K,\ldots,K])}{\tilde{q}_{t}([K,\ldots,K])}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{q}_{t}({\bm{y}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex80Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))/\tilde{Z}_{t}}=\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>numK</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}{\exp(-t\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))/\tilde{Z}_{t}}=\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}\not=[K,\ldots,K]}q_{t}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex80Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}=2\ln\left[1+(1+e^{-t})^{d}-1\right]\leq 2\cdot(1+e^{-t})^{d}-2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\ln\tilde{Z}_{t}=2\ln\left[1+(1+e^{-t})^{d}-1\right]\leq 2\cdot(1+e^{-t})^{d}-2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.8.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose we require the TV distance to be small enough, e.g.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left({\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}\big\|\tilde{q}_{t}\right)\leq\epsilon\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad(1+e^{-t})^{d}-1\leq\epsilon/2\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad d\ln(1+e^{-t})\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left({\bm{q}}^{\to}_{t}\big\|\tilde{q}_{t}\right)\leq\epsilon\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad(1+e^{-t})^{d}-1\leq\epsilon/2\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad d\ln(1+e^{-t})\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.9.1" class="ltx_text">then, since <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln(1+c)\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln(1+c)\leq c</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the sufficient condition for the establishment of the above equation is to require</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d\cdot e^{-t}\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2)\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad t\geq\ln(d/\ln(1+\epsilon/2))\quad\Leftarrow\quad t\geq\ln(4d/\epsilon)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇐</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\cdot e^{-t}\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2)\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad t\geq\ln(d/\ln(1+\epsilon/2))\quad\Leftarrow\quad t\geq\ln(4d/\epsilon),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.10.1" class="ltx_text">where the last derivation establishes since <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon/4\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon/4\leq\ln(1+\epsilon/2)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> without loss of generality.
Hence, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Euler Discretization Analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Assumption 2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al. [2025]</a></cite>, <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[A1]-</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score approximation error assumption</span>
The discrete score <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) is well-trained, and its estimation error satisfies for the chosen discretization step size <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=nh+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=nh+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T-\delta}\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\int_{kh}^{(k+1)h}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}R^{\to}({\mathbf{y}}_{t},{\bm{y}})D_{\phi}\left(v_{kh,{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}({\bm{y}})||\tilde{v}_{kh,{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}({\bm{y}})\right)\right]{\textnormal{d}}t\leq\epsilon_{score}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T-\delta}\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\int_{kh}^{(k+1)h}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{t}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}R^{\to}({\mathbf{y}}_{t},{\bm{y}})D_{\phi}\left(v_{kh,{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}({\bm{y}})||\tilde{v}_{kh,{\mathbf{y}}_{t}}({\bm{y}})\right)\right]{\textnormal{d}}t\leq\epsilon_{score}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ Theoretical results. ‣ 4 Euler Sampler in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the Euler-discretization update in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In Typical Euler samplers and their extensions. ‣ 4 Euler Sampler in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A3.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{Eu}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\propto\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{Eu}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\propto\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\Delta t\cdot R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, assume that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the two sufficient conditions of the transition rate matrix: its off-diagonal entries are non-negative, and each row sums to zero <span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">
                    †
                  †\dagger</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">
                    †
                  †\dagger</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math></span>
              
              
              
            Notice that our notation of <math id="footnote1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="footnote1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">transpose</span> of the convention used in some other works.</span></span></span>. In this way, both <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{h\tilde{R_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{h\tilde{R_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+h\tilde{R_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+h\tilde{R_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the transpose of valid transition matrices. The probability transition matrix of the Euler discretization can then be written as <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}=I+h\tilde{R}^{\top}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}=I+h\tilde{R}^{\top}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each element can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=q^{Eu}_{t+h|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+h\cdot\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=q^{Eu}_{t+h|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})=\delta_{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+h\cdot\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">To prove the convergence bound for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{\delta},q^{Eu}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{\delta},q^{Eu}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce an auxiliary process <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{EI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{EI}</annotation></semantics></math> using the exponential integrator update <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}=e^{h\tilde{R_{t}}^{\top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{Eu}_{t,t+h}=e^{h\tilde{R_{t}}^{\top}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. We first prove the bound for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{T-\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{T-\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> separately, and use the triangle inequality to conclude the proof. Take <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=nh+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=nh+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bound for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{T-\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{T-\delta},q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For time interval <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[kh,(k+1)h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[kh,(k+1)h]</annotation></semantics></math>, by the chain rule of TV distance (Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma E.5 (The chain rule of TV distance). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h},q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{kh},q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{Eu}_{kh}}\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}}),q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h},q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{kh},q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{Eu}_{kh}}\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}}),q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By the definition of total variation distance, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E41X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}}),q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}}),q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left|q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}\mid{\bm{y}})-q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}\mid{\bm{y}})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left|q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}\mid{\bm{y}})-q^{EI}_{(k+1)h\mid kh}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}\mid{\bm{y}})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E41Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left|Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}}\left|Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Writing out the difference between <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}=I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}=I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the Taylor series expansion for the matrix exponential:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}=I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}+\frac{1}{2!}h^{2}(\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{2}+\frac{1}{3!}h^{3}(\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{3}+\dots," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}=I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}+\frac{1}{2!}h^{2}(\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{2}+\frac{1}{3!}h^{3}(\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{3}+\dots,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}-\left(I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}\right)=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}=e^{h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}}-\left(I+h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top}\right)=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}(h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, by the triangle inequality, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\left((h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{i!}\left((h\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh}^{\top})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Tonelli’s theorem for series)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right|\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|(\tilde{R}_{kh})^{i}\right\|_{1}\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|^{i}_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\left((\tilde{R}_{kh})^{i}\right)({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right|\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|(\tilde{R}_{kh})^{i}\right\|_{1}\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|^{i}_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A\right\|_{1}=\max_{1\leq j\leq n}\sum_{i=1}^{m}|a_{i,j}|=\max_{x\neq\bm{0}}\left\|Ax\right\|_{1}/\left\|x\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A\right\|_{1}=\max_{1\leq j\leq n}\sum_{i=1}^{m}|a_{i,j}|=\max_{x\neq\bm{0}}\left\|Ax\right\|_{1}/\left\|x\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of the matrix. And the last inequality is due to the multiplicative property of this matrix norm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|^{i}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|Q^{EI}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})-Q^{Eu}_{kh,(k+1)h}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|\leq\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\frac{h^{i}}{i!}\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|^{i}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}}-1-h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}}-1-h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Plugging this into Eq. (<a href="#A3.E40" title="In Bound for TV(𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝑢}_{𝑇-𝛿},𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝐼}_{𝑇-𝛿}). ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Euler Discretization Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E41" title="In Bound for TV(𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝑢}_{𝑇-𝛿},𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝐼}_{𝑇-𝛿}). ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Euler Discretization Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E42X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h},q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{kh},q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{(k+1)h},q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{kh},q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By Assumption 2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al. [2025]</a></cite>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex94X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\tilde{R}_{t}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\tilde{R}_{t}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right|=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right|=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\left|R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex94Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\left((d-\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}}))+\sum_{\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\;\text{and}\;{\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}=K}\left|\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|\right){\textrm{(By Eq.\penalty\ \ref{eq:fwd_transtion_rate_func})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ham</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>DiffIdx</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>(By Eq. </mtext><mtext><a href="#S3.E7" title="In Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{{\bm{y}}}\left((d-\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}}))+\sum_{\mathrm{Ham}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=1\;\text{and}\;{\bm{y}}_{\mathrm{DiffIdx}\left({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\right)}=K}\left|\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right|\right){\textrm{(By Eq.\penalty\ \ref{eq:fwd_transtion_rate_func})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex94Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max_{{\bm{y}}}\left(d-\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}})+KdM\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max_{{\bm{y}}}\left(d-\mathrm{numK}({\bm{y}})+KdM\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex94Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2KdM." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2KdM.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Thus
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 2KdM" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\leq 2KdM</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#A3.E42" title="In Bound for TV(𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝑢}_{𝑇-𝛿},𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝐼}_{𝑇-𝛿}). ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Euler Discretization Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) we have</p>
<table id="A3.E43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E43X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{nh},q^{EI}_{nh}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{nh},q^{EI}_{nh}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{0},q^{EI}_{0}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{0},q^{EI}_{0}\right)+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(h\left\|\tilde{R}_{kh}\right\|_{1}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E43Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq K^{2}d^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{n}h^{2}M^{2}\leq K^{2}d^{2}nh^{2}M^{2}\leq K^{2}(T-\delta)hd^{2}M^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq K^{2}d^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{n}h^{2}M^{2}\leq K^{2}d^{2}nh^{2}M^{2}\leq K^{2}(T-\delta)hd^{2}M^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By taking <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{K^{2}d^{2}M^{2}\log(d/\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{K^{2}d^{2}M^{2}\log(d/\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{nh},q^{EI}_{nh}\right)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{Eu}_{nh},q^{EI}_{nh}\right)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bound for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{EI}_{T-\delta},q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{EI}_{T-\delta},q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|q^{EI}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, then use Pinsker’s inequality to derive the bound for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{EI}_{T-\delta},q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{EI}_{T-\delta},q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For time interval <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[kh,(k+1)h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[kh,(k+1)h]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{(k+1)h}\big\|q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)=\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{kh}\big\|q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\int_{kh}^{(k+1)h}\frac{{\textnormal{d}}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)}{{\textnormal{d}}t}{\textnormal{d}}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext>d</mtext><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{(k+1)h}\big\|q^{EI}_{(k+1)h}\right)=\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{kh}\big\|q^{EI}_{kh}\right)+\int_{kh}^{(k+1)h}\frac{{\textnormal{d}}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)}{{\textnormal{d}}t}{\textnormal{d}}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By the chain rule of KL divergence (Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma E.4 (The chain rule of KL divergence). ‣ Appendix E Technical Lemmas ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.4</span></a>)</p>
<table id="A3.E45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E45X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\textnormal{d}}}{{\textnormal{d}}t}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mtext>d</mtext><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\textnormal{d}}}{{\textnormal{d}}t}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t}\right)-\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)}{\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t}\right)-\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t}\big\|q^{EI}_{t}\right)}{\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E45Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)}{\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)}{\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E45Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\underbrace{\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)}{\Delta t}}_{\textrm{Term }1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Term </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t}}\underbrace{\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\big\|q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t\mid t}(\cdot\mid{\bm{y}})\right)}{\Delta t}}_{\textrm{Term }1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we focus on Term 1 of Eq. (<a href="#A3.E45" title="In Bound for TV(𝑞^{𝐸⁢𝐼}_{𝑇-𝛿},𝑞^←_{𝑇-𝛿}). ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Euler Discretization Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>), and have</p>
<table id="A3.E46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E46X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>Term 1</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\Delta t^{-1}\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\Delta t^{-1}\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E46Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\cdot\ln\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}\right]}_{\text{Term 1.1}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 1.1</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{\Delta t}\cdot\ln\frac{q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}{q^{EI}_{t+\Delta t|t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}})}\right]}_{\text{Term 1.1}}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
