<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.14.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equation follows from Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1 (Adapted from Eqs. (3) and (4) of ( ) ). ‣ The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E58" title="In D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>).
For Term 1.2, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E63X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 1.2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Term 1.2</mtext><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 1.2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E63Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\Delta t^{-1}\cdot\ln\frac{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})}{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\hat{q}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]\leq 1\cdot(\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot\lim_{\Delta t\rightarrow 0}\left[\Delta t^{-1}\cdot\ln\frac{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})}{1-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\hat{q}_{t+\Delta t|t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime}|{\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]\leq 1\cdot(\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.15.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>.
Plugging Eq. (<a href="#A4.E62" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A4.E63" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E61" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>), into Eq. (<a href="#A4.E60" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E64X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{0}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\big\|\hat{q}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\right)\right]/\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{0}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\big\|\hat{q}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\right)\right]/\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E64Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}q^{\leftarrow}_{t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})}q^{\leftarrow}_{t,t_{w-1}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}_{0})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.16.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for any <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E65X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E65Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\ln\frac{R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\ln\frac{R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E65Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{+\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\ln\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}_{\text{Term 2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ln</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 2</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{+\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\ln\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}_{\text{Term 2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.17.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, due to Eq. (<a href="#S5.E18" title="In Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\quad\text{and}\quad\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\quad\text{and}\quad\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})=\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.18.1" class="ltx_text">which implies <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Term 2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Term 2</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Term 2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A4.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>).
Otherwise, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}=\frac{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}=\frac{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}=\frac{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\hat{R}_{t,{\bm{y}}_{0}}({\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}=\frac{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.19.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex133X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>Term 2</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex133Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\left[1+\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\left[1+\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex133Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})\cdot\left[\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})\cdot\left[\frac{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}{\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})}\right]+\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})-\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.20.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)\leq\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}_{0}\right)\quad\Rightarrow\quad R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{0}\in{\mathcal{Y}}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)\leq\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}_{0}\right)\quad\Rightarrow\quad R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\leq\beta_{t_{w}}({\bm{y}}_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.21.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with Eq. (<a href="#A4.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E64" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E66X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{0}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\big\|\hat{q}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\right)\right]/\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}_{0}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\big\|\hat{q}_{t|t_{w-1}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{y}}_{0})\right)\right]/\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E66Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}})-R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E66Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\left(\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\cdot\ln\frac{R_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}{\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})}+\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}\tilde{R}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})-\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}}^{\prime},{\bm{y}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E66Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\left[-\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}+\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot\left[-\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}+\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})+\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\ln\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E66Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})D_{\mathrm{\phi}}\left(\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\big\|\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}}}q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})\cdot\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\neq{\bm{y}}}R^{\to}({\bm{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})D_{\mathrm{\phi}}\left(\frac{q_{t}^{\leftarrow}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})}{q^{\leftarrow}_{t}({\bm{y}})}\big\|\tilde{v}_{t,{\bm{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.22.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Bregman divergence with <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(c)=c\ln c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(c)=c\ln c</annotation></semantics></math> (as Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In The reverse process notations. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)), and the last equation follows from the definition of Bregman divergence:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\phi}(u\|v)=\phi(u)-\phi(v)-\langle\nabla\phi(v),u-v\rangle=u\ln\frac{u}{v}-u+v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>ln</mi><mfrac><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\phi}(u\|v)=\phi(u)-\phi(v)-\langle\nabla\phi(v),u-v\rangle=u\ln\frac{u}{v}-u+v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.23.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, Eq. (<a href="#A4.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) can be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w}}\big\|\hat{q}_{t_{w}}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\big\|\hat{q}_{t_{w-1}}\right)+\int_{t_{w-1}}^{t_{w}}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}\sim q^{\to}_{T-t}}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\mathbf{y}}}R^{\to}({\mathbf{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot D_{\mathrm{\phi}}\left(v_{t,{\mathbf{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\big\|\tilde{v}_{t,{\mathbf{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w}}\big\|\hat{q}_{t_{w}}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\big\|\hat{q}_{t_{w-1}}\right)+\int_{t_{w-1}}^{t_{w}}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{y}}\sim q^{\to}_{T-t}}\left[\sum_{{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\not={\mathbf{y}}}R^{\to}({\mathbf{y}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\cdot D_{\mathrm{\phi}}\left(v_{t,{\mathbf{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\big\|\tilde{v}_{t,{\mathbf{y}}}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.24.1" class="ltx_text">With a recursive manner, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex137" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex137X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex137X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{0}\big\|\hat{q}_{0}\right)+L_{\text{SE}}(\tilde{v})=\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\to}_{T}\big\|\hat{q}_{0}\right)+L_{\text{SE}}(\tilde{v})\leq(1+e^{-T})^{d}-1+T\epsilon^{2}_{\text{score}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>SE</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>SE</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>score</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{0}\big\|\hat{q}_{0}\right)+L_{\text{SE}}(\tilde{v})=\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\to}_{T}\big\|\hat{q}_{0}\right)+L_{\text{SE}}(\tilde{v})\leq(1+e^{-T})^{d}-1+T\epsilon^{2}_{\text{score}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.25.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1 (Exponentially decreasing KL divergence between 𝑞^→_𝑡 and 𝑞̃_𝑡). ‣ Masked discrete diffusion instantiation and approximation. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#S2.I1.i1" title="item [A1] ‣ General Assumptions. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">[A1]</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{q}_{0}({\bm{y}})=\tilde{q}_{T}({\bm{y}})\propto\exp(-T\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>numK</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{0}({\bm{y}})=\tilde{q}_{T}({\bm{y}})\propto\exp(-T\cdot(d-\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.26.1" class="ltx_text">If we set</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T\geq\ln(4d/\epsilon^{2})\quad\text{and}\quad\epsilon_{\text{score}}\leq T^{-1/2}\cdot\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>score</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq\ln(4d/\epsilon^{2})\quad\text{and}\quad\epsilon_{\text{score}}\leq T^{-1/2}\cdot\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.27.1" class="ltx_text">it has <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+e^{-T})^{d}-1\leq\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+e^{-T})^{d}-1\leq\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\epsilon^{2}_{\text{score}}\leq\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>score</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\epsilon^{2}_{\text{score}}\leq\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq 2\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq 2\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounding <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the proof strategy of Theorem 6 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen and Ying [2024]</a></cite>.
Consider the forward process <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the coupling characterization of the total variation distance, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)\coloneqq\inf_{\gamma\in\Gamma(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})}\mathbb{P}_{(u,v)\sim\gamma}[u\neq v]\leq\mathbb{P}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)\coloneqq\inf_{\gamma\in\Gamma(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})}\mathbb{P}_{(u,v)\sim\gamma}[u\neq v]\leq\mathbb{P}({\mathbf{y}}\neq{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all couplings of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the inequality holds because <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{y}},{\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> gives a coupling of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Without loss of generality, we suppose <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\to}_{0}({\bm{y}})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\to}_{0}({\bm{y}})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then,
combining the transition kernel given Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5 (Forward transition kernel). ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="item [A2] ‣ Additional settings. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">[A2]</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex141" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex141X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0}q^{\to}_{0}[{\bm{y}}]\cdot q^{\to}_{\delta|0}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0}q_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot e^{-\delta d}=e^{-\delta d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}({\mathbf{y}}={\mathbf{y}}^{\prime})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0}q^{\to}_{0}[{\bm{y}}]\cdot q^{\to}_{\delta|0}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathcal{Y}},\mathrm{numK}\left({\bm{y}}\right)=0}q_{0}^{\to}({\bm{y}})\cdot e^{-\delta d}=e^{-\delta d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, by choosing <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leq\epsilon/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leq\epsilon/d</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leq d^{-1}\epsilon\leq d^{-1}\cdot\ln\left(\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}\right)\quad\Rightarrow\quad e^{\delta d}\leq\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)\leq 1-e^{-\delta d}\leq\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leq d^{-1}\epsilon\leq d^{-1}\cdot\ln\left(\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}\right)\quad\Rightarrow\quad e^{\delta d}\leq\frac{1}{1-\epsilon}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{*},q^{\to}_{\delta}\right)\leq 1-e^{-\delta d}\leq\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Finally, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{0}^{\to},\hat{q}^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{0}^{\to},q_{\delta}^{\to}\right)+\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{T-\delta}^{\leftarrow},\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\epsilon+\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)}\leq 2\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{0}^{\to},\hat{q}^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{0}^{\to},q_{\delta}^{\to}\right)+\mathrm{TV}\left(q_{T-\delta}^{\leftarrow},\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)\leq\epsilon+\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{KL}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-\delta}\big\|\hat{q}_{T-\delta}\right)}\leq 2\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Hence the proof is completed.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>The complexity of Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The complexity of Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumption <a href="#S2.I1.i1" title="item [A1] ‣ General Assumptions. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">[A1]</span></a> and <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="item [A2] ‣ Additional settings. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">[A2]</span></a> hold, following from the settings shown in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem D.4 (The convergence of Alg. ). ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, if we implement Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{w}-t_{w-1}=\eta\quad\text{where}\quad w\in\{1,2,\ldots W\},\quad W=(T-\delta)/\eta,\quad\eta=\epsilon/2d,\quad\text{and}\quad\epsilon&lt;1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{w}-t_{w-1}=\eta\quad\text{where}\quad w\in\{1,2,\ldots W\},\quad W=(T-\delta)/\eta,\quad\eta=\epsilon/2d,\quad\text{and}\quad\epsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the expectation of iteration/score estimation complexity of Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Mask-aware truncation and algorithm proposal. ‣ 5 Truncated Uniformization in Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> will be upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2K(d-\epsilon^{2}/4)+12Kd\ln d" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2K(d-\epsilon^{2}/4)+12Kd\ln d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">to achieve <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{*},\hat{p}\right)\leq 2\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{*},\hat{p}\right)\leq 2\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the underlying distribution of generated samples.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">We denote <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> to present the reverse process.
For a specific trajectory, e.g., <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}=\{\hat{{\bm{y}}}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}=\{\hat{{\bm{y}}}\}_{t=0}^{T-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total expected iteration number will be equivalent to the summation of Poisson expectations of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> segments, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})=\frac{K\cdot\mathrm{numK}\left(\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{t_{w-1}}\right)}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})=\frac{K\cdot\mathrm{numK}\left(\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{t_{w-1}}\right)}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">which means the expected iteration number of the reverse process can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A4.E68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E68X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]=\sum_{w=1}^{W}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]\cdot\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]=\sum_{w=1}^{W}\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]\cdot\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">Although <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]</annotation></semantics></math> is respect to the practical distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}}\sim\hat{q}_{t_{w-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}}\sim\hat{q}_{t_{w-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can approximate it by the forward marginal distribution, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]=\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]\quad\text{where}\quad{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\ \text{and}\ {\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}}\sim q^{\to}_{t_{w-1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]=\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]\quad\text{where}\quad{\mathbf{y}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\sim q^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}}\ \text{and}\ {\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}}\sim q^{\to}_{t_{w-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, with Assumption <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="item [A2] ‣ Additional settings. ‣ 3 The Forward Process of Masked Discrete Diffusion ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">[A2]</span></a>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}_{0}^{\to}\right)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}_{0}^{\to}\right)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under this condition, the transition kernel becomes</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex147" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex147X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex147X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{\to}_{t|0}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=\prod_{i=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex147X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\underbrace{\left(1-{\bm{1}}_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot{\bm{1}}_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-t}}_{\text{remain non-mask token}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>remain non-mask token</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\underbrace{\left(1-{\bm{1}}_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot{\bm{1}}_{0}({\bm{y}}_{i}-{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\cdot e^{-t}}_{\text{remain non-mask token}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex147Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex147Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\underbrace{\left(1-{\bm{1}}_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-t})}_{\text{turn into mask token}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>turn into mask token</mtext></msub><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\underbrace{\left(1-{\bm{1}}_{(K,K)}({\bm{y}}_{i},{\bm{y}}_{i}^{\prime})\right)\cdot{\bm{1}}_{K}({\bm{y}}_{i})\cdot(1-e^{-t})}_{\text{turn into mask token}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text">due to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5 (Forward transition kernel). ‣ B.3 The Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B The Markov Processes of Discrete Diffusion Models ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.
Let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>numK</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability that exactly <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> out of the <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates are mask tokens (<math id="A4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>) at time <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because each of the <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates evolves independently (and identically, each with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math> of being the mask token at time <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>), we get a standard Binomial random variable:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each coordinate is <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each coordinate is non-<math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.13.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]=C_{d}^{k}\cdot(1-e^{-t})^{k}\cdot(e^{-t})^{d-k}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]=d\cdot(1-e^{-t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>numK</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mtext>and</mtext><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>numK</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]=C_{d}^{k}\cdot(1-e^{-t})^{k}\cdot(e^{-t})^{d-k}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}\left({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{t}\right)=k]=d\cdot(1-e^{-t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.14.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for any <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]=d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]=d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the settings shown in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem D.4 (The convergence of Alg. ). ‣ D.2 The convergence of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{w-1}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{w-1}}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{W}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{W}}\right)\leq 2\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{w-1}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{w-1}}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{W}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{W}}\right)\leq 2\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.15.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({{\mathbf{y}}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]\right|\leq d\cdot\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{w-1}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{w-1}}\right)\leq 2d\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({{\mathbf{y}}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]\right|\leq d\cdot\mathrm{TV}\left(q^{\leftarrow}_{T-t_{w-1}},\hat{q}_{T-t_{w-1}}\right)\leq 2d\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.16.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E69X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]\leq\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({{\mathbf{y}}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]+2d\epsilon=\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]+2d\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>numK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})]\leq\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({{\mathbf{y}}}^{\leftarrow}_{t_{w-1}})]+2d\epsilon=\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{numK}({\mathbf{y}}^{\to}_{T-t_{w-1}})]+2d\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E69Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})+2d\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})+2d\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.17.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging Eq. (<a href="#A4.E69" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) into Eq. (<a href="#A4.E68" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E70X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E70Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{w=1}^{W}d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{w=1}^{W}d\cdot(1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})})\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E70Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{w=1}^{W}2d\epsilon\cdot\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{w=1}^{W}2d\epsilon\cdot\frac{K}{e^{(T-t_{w})}-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E70Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-t_{w})}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\cdot\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}}_{\text{Term 1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 1</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-t_{w})}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\cdot\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}}_{\text{Term 1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E70Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{2Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\left(e^{T-t_{w}}-1\right)^{-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})}_{\text{Term 2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Term 2</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{2Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\left(e^{T-t_{w}}-1\right)^{-1}\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})}_{\text{Term 2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.18.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we suppose the segments share the same length <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{w}-t_{w-1}=\eta\quad\text{where}\quad w\in\{1,2,\ldots W\},\quad W=(T-\delta)/\eta,\quad\text{and}\quad\eta=\epsilon/2d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{w}-t_{w-1}=\eta\quad\text{where}\quad w\in\{1,2,\ldots W\},\quad W=(T-\delta)/\eta,\quad\text{and}\quad\eta=\epsilon/2d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.19.1" class="ltx_text">Under these conditions, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E71X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta\leq\frac{\delta}{2}\leq\ln(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{e^{\delta}}{2})\quad\Rightarrow\quad e^{\eta}\leq\frac{e^{\delta}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\leq\frac{e^{(T-t_{w-1})}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\quad\forall\ w\in\{1,\ldots,W\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta\leq\frac{\delta}{2}\leq\ln(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{e^{\delta}}{2})\quad\Rightarrow\quad e^{\eta}\leq\frac{e^{\delta}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\leq\frac{e^{(T-t_{w-1})}}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\quad\forall\ w\in\{1,\ldots,W\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E71Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad e^{\eta}\leq\frac{1+e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{2e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}\quad\Rightarrow\quad 2\cdot e^{-(T-t_{w-1}-\eta)}\leq 1+e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad e^{\eta}\leq\frac{1+e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{2e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}\quad\Rightarrow\quad 2\cdot e^{-(T-t_{w-1}-\eta)}\leq 1+e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E71Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad 1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}\leq 2-2e^{-(T-t_{w-1}-\eta)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}\leq 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad 1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}\leq 2-2e^{-(T-t_{w-1}-\eta)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}\leq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.20.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging these results into Term 1 of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E72X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 1}=2Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-t_{w})}\cdot\eta=2Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-w\eta)}\cdot\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Term 1</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 1}=2Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-t_{w})}\cdot\eta=2Kd\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}e^{-(T-w\eta)}\cdot\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E72Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2Kd\cdot\eta\cdot e^{-T}\cdot\frac{e^{(W+1)\eta}-e^{\eta}}{e^{\eta}-1}\leq 2Kd\cdot e^{\eta}\cdot\left(e^{-\delta}-e^{-T}\right)\leq 2Kd\cdot(1-e^{-T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2Kd\cdot\eta\cdot e^{-T}\cdot\frac{e^{(W+1)\eta}-e^{\eta}}{e^{\eta}-1}\leq 2Kd\cdot e^{\eta}\cdot\left(e^{-\delta}-e^{-T}\right)\leq 2Kd\cdot(1-e^{-T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E72Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2Kd\cdot\left(1-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{4d}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2Kd\cdot\left(1-\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{4d}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.21.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex152" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex152X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex152X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{e^{T-t_{w-1}}-1}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}=\frac{e^{T-t_{w-1}}}{e^{T-t_{w}}}\cdot\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}\leq e^{\eta}\cdot 2\leq 2e," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>η</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{e^{T-t_{w-1}}-1}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}=\frac{e^{T-t_{w-1}}}{e^{T-t_{w}}}\cdot\frac{1-e^{-(T-t_{w-1})}}{1-e^{-(T-t_{w})}}\leq e^{\eta}\cdot 2\leq 2e,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.22.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E71" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) and the last inequality is established when <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, Term 2 of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) can be upper bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A4.E73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E73X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 2}=2Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}\leq 4e\cdot Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{e^{T-t_{w-1}}-1}\leq 4e\cdot Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{T-t_{w-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Term 2</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 2}=2Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{e^{T-t_{w}}-1}\leq 4e\cdot Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{e^{T-t_{w-1}}-1}\leq 4e\cdot Kd\epsilon\cdot\sum_{w=1}^{W}\frac{\eta}{T-t_{w-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E73Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\int_{0}^{T-\delta}\frac{1}{T-t}\mathrm{d}t=4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\ln\frac{T}{\delta}\leq 4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\ln\frac{4d^{2}}{\epsilon^{3}}\leq 12e\cdot Kd\ln d\cdot\epsilon\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\int_{0}^{T-\delta}\frac{1}{T-t}\mathrm{d}t=4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\ln\frac{T}{\delta}\leq 4e\cdot dK\epsilon\cdot\ln\frac{4d^{2}}{\epsilon^{3}}\leq 12e\cdot Kd\ln d\cdot\epsilon\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.23.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\leq d\quad\text{and}\quad\ln\frac{d^{3}}{\epsilon^{3}}=3\ln\frac{d}{\epsilon}\leq 3\ln d\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\leq d\quad\text{and}\quad\ln\frac{d^{3}}{\epsilon^{3}}=3\ln\frac{d}{\epsilon}\leq 3\ln d\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.24.1" class="ltx_text">without loss of generality.
Moreover, when <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}\leq e^{-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\ln\frac{1}{\epsilon}\leq e^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.25.1" class="ltx_text">which follows from the monotonicity of the function <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\ln x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\ln x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under this condition, the RHS of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E73" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) has the following bound</span></p>
<table id="A4.E74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E74X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Term 2}\leq 12\cdot Kd\ln d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Term 2</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Term 2}\leq 12\cdot Kd\ln d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.26.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, plugging Eq. (<a href="#A4.E72" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E74" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) into Eq. (<a href="#A4.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 The complexity of Alg. ‣ Appendix D Truncated Uniformization Inference Analysis ‣ On the Complexity Theory of Masked Discrete Diffusion: From poly(1/ϵ) to Nearly ϵ-Free" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), the expected calls of discrete scores will be</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]\leq 2K(d-\epsilon^{2})+12Kd\ln d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{w=1}^{W}\beta_{t_{w}}(\hat{{\mathbf{y}}}_{t_{w-1}})\cdot(t_{w}-t_{w-1})\right]\leq 2K(d-\epsilon^{2})+12Kd\ln d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.27.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the proof is completed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Technical Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Basic Kronecker product)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Supppose the Kronecker product for <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> matrices defined on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\bm{A}}}\coloneqq{\bm{A}}_{1}\otimes{\bm{A}}_{2}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{A}}_{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\bm{A}}}\coloneqq{\bm{A}}_{1}\otimes{\bm{A}}_{2}\otimes\ldots\otimes{\bm{A}}_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\bm{A}}}_{[a_{1,i},a_{2,i},\ldots,a_{n,i}],[a_{1,j},a_{2,j},\ldots,a_{n,j}]}\coloneqq\overline{{\bm{A}}}_{\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{k,i}\cdot d^{n-k},\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{k,j}\cdot d^{n-k}}=\prod_{k=1}^{n}[{\bm{A}}_{k}]_{a_{k,i},a_{k,j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\bm{A}}}_{[a_{1,i},a_{2,i},\ldots,a_{n,i}],[a_{1,j},a_{2,j},\ldots,a_{n,j}]}\coloneqq\overline{{\bm{A}}}_{\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{k,i}\cdot d^{n-k},\sum_{k=1}^{n}a_{k,j}\cdot d^{n-k}}=\prod_{k=1}^{n}[{\bm{A}}_{k}]_{a_{k,i},a_{k,j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">This lemma can easily be proved by the definition of Kronecker product.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mixed-product property of Kronecker product)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the matrices <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}},{\bm{B}},{\bm{C}},{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}},{\bm{B}},{\bm{C}},{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then, the products <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> are well-defined. We have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})=({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})=({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this by examining the product on the left-hand side, <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
and showing it coincides block-by-block with <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We starts from the definition of Kronecker products in blocks.
By definition, the Kronecker product <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be seen as an <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d\times d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d\times d)</annotation></semantics></math> block matrix
in which the <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-th block is <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}\,{\bm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}\,{\bm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\;=\;\begin{pmatrix}a_{11}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{12}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{1n}{\bm{B}}\\[4.0pt]
a_{21}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{22}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{2n}{\bm{B}}\\[4.0pt]
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\[4.0pt]
a_{m1}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{m2}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{mn}{\bm{B}}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}}\;=\;\begin{pmatrix}a_{11}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{12}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{1n}{\bm{B}}\\[4.0pt]
a_{21}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{22}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{2n}{\bm{B}}\\[4.0pt]
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\[4.0pt]
a_{m1}{\bm{B}}&amp;a_{m2}{\bm{B}}&amp;\cdots&amp;a_{mn}{\bm{B}}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\;=\;\begin{pmatrix}c_{11}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{12}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{1r}{\bm{D}}\\[4.0pt]
c_{21}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{22}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{2r}{\bm{D}}\\[4.0pt]
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\[4.0pt]
c_{n1}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{n2}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{nr}{\bm{D}}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\;=\;\begin{pmatrix}c_{11}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{12}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{1r}{\bm{D}}\\[4.0pt]
c_{21}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{22}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{2r}{\bm{D}}\\[4.0pt]
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\[4.0pt]
c_{n1}{\bm{D}}&amp;c_{n2}{\bm{D}}&amp;\cdots&amp;c_{nr}{\bm{D}}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we form the Product <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
When multiplying two block matrices, we sum over the matching inner block dimensions. Specifically,
the <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-block of <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}\Bigl(\,(a_{ij}{\bm{B}})\,\bigl(c_{jk}{\bm{D}}\bigr)\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}\Bigl(\,(a_{ij}{\bm{B}})\,\bigl(c_{jk}{\bm{D}}\bigr)\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Inside each term, we treat <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}\,{\bm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}\,{\bm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{jk}\,{\bm{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{jk}\,{\bm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> as scalar-matrix products. We can rewrite
the expression as:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}\,a_{ij}\,c_{jk}\;\Bigl({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}\Bigr)\;=\;\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{ij}\,c_{jk}\Bigr)\;{\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}\,a_{ij}\,c_{jk}\;\Bigl({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}\Bigr)\;=\;\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{ij}\,c_{jk}\Bigr)\;{\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that the factor <math id="A5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{ij}\,c_{jk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{ij}\,c_{jk}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="A5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-th
entry of the matrix product <math id="A5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}{\bm{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}{\bm{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, each <math id="A5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-block of <math id="A5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>
simplifies to</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}\;({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}\;({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now observe that the Kronecker product <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> can also be viewed as an
<math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m\times r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m\times r)</annotation></semantics></math> block matrix whose <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-th block is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}\;({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})_{ik}\;({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-th block of <math id="A5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> matches exactly with the <math id="A5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>-th block
we computed for <math id="A5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since these two matrices agree in every block of a <math id="A5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{2}\times d^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{2}\times d^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> partition, we conclude</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})\;=\;({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{A}}\otimes{\bm{B}})\,({\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}})\;=\;({\bm{A}}{\bm{C}})\otimes({\bm{B}}{\bm{D}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Kolmogorov backward theorem, adapted from Theorem 5.11 in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Särkkä and Solin [2019]</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a specific SDE, if we denote the transition density from <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{y}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{y}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)</annotation></semantics></math>
, then it solves the backward Kolmogorov equation</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\frac{\partial p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)}{\partial s}={\mathcal{L}}p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{\partial p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)}{\partial s}={\mathcal{L}}p({\bm{y}},t|{\bm{x}},s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the infinitesimal operator of the SDE.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The chain rule of KL divergence)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider four random variables, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}},\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}},\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose underlying distributions are denoted as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{x},p_{z},q_{x},q_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{x},p_{z},q_{x},q_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{x,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{x,z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{x,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{x,z}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the densities of joint distributions of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we write in terms of the conditionals and marginals as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex167" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex167X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex167X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=p_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot p_{z}({\bm{z}})=p_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{x}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=p_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot p_{z}({\bm{z}})=p_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{x}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex167Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex167Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=q_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot q_{z}({\bm{z}})=q_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot q_{x}({\bm{x}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=q_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot q_{z}({\bm{z}})=q_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot q_{x}({\bm{x}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex168" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex168X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex168X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x,z}\big\|q_{x,z}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x,z}\big\|q_{x,z}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex168X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{z}\big\|q_{z}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{z}}\sim p_{z}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\big\|q_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{z}\big\|q_{z}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{z}}\sim p_{z}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\big\|q_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex168Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex168Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex168Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x}\big\|q_{x}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}}\sim p_{x}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\big\|q_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x}\big\|q_{x}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}}\sim p_{x}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\big\|q_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the latter equation implies</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x}\big\|q_{x}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x,z}\big\|q_{x,z}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x}\big\|q_{x}\right)\leq\mathrm{KL}\left(p_{x,z}\big\|q_{x,z}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The chain rule of TV distance)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider four random variables, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}},\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}},\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose underlying distributions are denoted as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{x},p_{z},q_{x},q_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{x},p_{z},q_{x},q_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{x,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{x,z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{x,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{x,z}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the densities of joint distributions of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{z}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{{\mathbf{x}}},\tilde{{\mathbf{z}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we write in terms of the conditionals and marginals as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex170" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex170X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex170X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=p_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot p_{z}({\bm{z}})=p_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{x}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=p_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot p_{z}({\bm{z}})=p_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{x}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex170Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex170Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=q_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot q_{z}({\bm{z}})=q_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot q_{x}({\bm{x}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{x,z}({\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=q_{x|z}({\bm{x}}|{\bm{z}})\cdot q_{z}({\bm{z}})=q_{z|x}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot q_{x}({\bm{x}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex171" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex171X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex171X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x,z},q_{x,z}\right)\leq\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x,z},q_{x,z}\right)\leq\min</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex171X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{z},q_{z}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{z}}\sim p_{z}}\left[\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}}),q_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\right)\right],\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{z},q_{z}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{z}}\sim p_{z}}\left[\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}}),q_{x|z}(\cdot|{\mathbf{z}})\right)\right],\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex171Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex171Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x},q_{x}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}}\sim p_{x}}\left[\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}}),q_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\right)\right]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x},q_{x}\right)+\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}}\sim p_{x}}\left[\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}}),q_{z|x}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}})\right)\right]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Besides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x},q_{x}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x,z},q_{x,z}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x},q_{x}\right)\leq\mathrm{TV}\left(p_{x,z},q_{x,z}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
